  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Hii Mission Technologies obligated $970M in FY2026 to date across 78 awards, with an average award size of $12.4M. Hii Mission Technologies obligations are down 16.4% year over year. Hii Mission Technologies saw larger prior-year totals, including $1.2B in FY25 and $1.1B in FY24, after several years around the $595M to $657M range from FY21 through FY23. Hii Mission Technologies work for federal buyers is concentrated: the General Services Administration obligated $773M and the Department of Defense obligated $196M in FY2026 to date. Hii Mission Technologies sells across a mix of NAICS markets; All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services accounted for $533M and Engineering Services accounted for $396M in FY2026 to date. Hii Mission Technologies also had smaller obligations in aviation-related and technical categories, including Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $29.7M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $5.3M. Current-year totals are partial, and the note for the period clarifies that figures are contract obligations except where award-value figures are noted in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Hii Mission Technologies main federal buyers?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the top buyer, obligating $773M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the second-largest buyer, obligating $196M. Other federal buyers show much smaller obligations, including the Department of the Interior at $443K and the Department of Education at $388K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services does Hii Mission Technologies provide?",
        "body": "All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services is the largest market for Hii Mission Technologies at $533M in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services is also a major market at $396M. Hii Mission Technologies has additional activity in aviation-support and technical niches, including Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $29.7M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $5.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
